From: webmaster@rapidcow.org
Date: Sun, 08 Jun 2025 23:37:46 +0800
Subject: Renewed!

Phew we're back... I guess.  All it took was an extra
"listen [::]:80" because Certbot really was adamant
about checking if my server was reachable via IPv6.
I guess it's because IPv6 didn't match any of the nginx
virtual server blocks so it went straight to my catch-all
fallback server that USUALLY denies requests that don't
provide an HTTP/1.1 Host header... but this time it
denied valid requests that simply use IPv6 and not the
IPv4 it knows.

I'm just, so weirded out -- like what @_@  Either way uh
I ran certbot renew and the post-renewal hook basically
brought all the sites back (it did completely ignore that
my pre-renewal hook complained with an error code, but...
whatever i guess &gt;_&gt;)  Right now I'm just reeling in
the madness i just witnessed, of my own site falling apart
completely because i didn't take that Let's Encrypt email
about expiration (that i did NOT expect was due to the
auto-renewal not running correctly!) so seriously.....

But well, lesson learned: Certbot does look at your IPv6.
I won't be dismissing that tiny [::]:80 and tiny [::]:443
anymore from now on....
